% The bibliography. Everything on /publications/ is derived from this file.
%
% Three of the fields used below are Studia Theme's, not BibTeX's. They are
% stripped from the citation a reader copies, and each is checked at build time:
%
%   abbr   the venue badge, looked up in src/data/venues.yml. An abbr with no
%          row there fails the build. Leave it out — as the last entry does —
%          and the publication simply renders without a badge.
%   pdf    a file under public/assets/pdf/, or an absolute URL. A relative path
%          that is not on disk fails the build.
%   page   this work's own page, /papers/<slug>/. It must have a matching
%          src/content/papers/<slug>.md, or the build fails.
%
% See docs/Content.md. The wiring is in src/content.config.ts.
%
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% DEMO CONTENT — replace the whole file.
%
% The works of Marcus Tullius Cicero (106-43 BC), cited the way a classicist
% actually would: the entry is the modern critical edition or translation, so
% `year` is the edition's and the ancient composition date goes in `note`.
% That also keeps the year buckets on /publications/ sensible, which "45 BC"
% would not.
%
% The DOIs use the 10.5555 prefix, which the DOI registry reserves for
% examples. They are syntactically valid and cannot collide with a real record,
% so the DOI chips here have something to render — but `npm run bib:check`
% will report them as not found at Crossref. That is correct: they are not
% registered. Replace them along with everything else.
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


